{"id":"claim:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--adnominal-definition-exclusive-noun-modifier","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topics":["topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--adnoun-diagnostics"],"statement":{"en":"Words that always precede a noun and function exclusively to modify nouns are defined as adnominals.","ja":"常に名詞に先行し、専ら名詞を修飾する機能のみをもつ語が連体詞と定義される。"},"type":"terminology","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:murasaki2025@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0031-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--adnominal-distributional-properties","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topics":["topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--adnoun-diagnostics"],"statement":{"en":"Adnominals do not serve as predicates or verb arguments, modify noun phrases, and take no personal affixes.","ja":"連体詞は述語や動詞の項にならず、名詞句を修飾し、人称接辞をとらない。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0114-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--oar-adnominal-and-adverbial-dual-function","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topics":["topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--adnoun-diagnostics"],"statement":{"en":"The general adnominal oar functions both as an adnominal and as an adverb.","ja":"一般連体詞 oar は連体詞としても副詞としても機能する。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/saru"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["oar","oar tek","oar isam"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0283-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--sonno-sino-dual-adnominal-adverbial-function","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topics":["topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--adnoun-diagnostics"],"statement":{"en":"The words sonno and sino can function both as adnominals meaning 'real/true' and as adverbs.","ja":"sonno と sino は「本当の」を意味する連体詞としても副詞としても機能する。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/saru","doculect:hokkaido/chitose"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["sonno","sino"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0283-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--adnouns-distinguished-by-inability-to-predicate","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topics":["topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--adnoun-diagnostics"],"statement":{"en":"Adnouns are distinguished from verbal modifiers by their inability to occur in predicate position.","ja":"連体詞は述語位置に立ち得ないことによって動詞的修飾語と区別される。"},"type":"membership","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["pirka","sino"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0146-08","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--adnoun-distribution-and-modification-properties","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topics":["topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--adnoun-diagnostics"],"statement":{"en":"Adnouns modify nouns and occasionally nominalizers, precede the noun, and cannot occur in predicate position.","ja":"連体詞は名詞や場合により名詞化辞を修飾し、名詞に先行し、述語位置に立つことができない。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["sino"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0147-06","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"refines","claim":"claim:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--adnouns-distinguished-by-inability-to-predicate","differs_in":"scope","note":"Refsing's fuller characterization of adnouns adds modifier distribution to the negative predicate diagnostic."}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--sonno-lacks-personal-affixes-unlike-verbs","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topics":["topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--adverb-diagnostics"],"statement":{"en":"The adverb sonno does not take person affixes, in contrast to intransitive verbs like sunke.","ja":"副詞 sonno は人称接辞を取らないが、自動詞 sunke は人称接辞をとる。"},"type":"membership","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"specific","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["sonno","sunke"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:murasaki2025@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0112-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--adverb-distributional-properties","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topics":["topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--adverb-diagnostics"],"statement":{"en":"Adverbs do not serve as predicates or verb arguments, modify verb phrases, and take objective personal affixes if any.","ja":"副詞は述語や動詞の項にならず、動詞句を修飾し、人称接辞をとる場合は目的格をとる。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0114-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--postpositional-adverbs-lack-nominative-affixes","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topics":["topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--adverb-diagnostics"],"statement":{"en":"Verbs converted into postpositional adverbs do not take nominative personal affixes.","ja":"後置副詞に転換した動詞は主格人称接辞をとらない。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0120-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--usa-adverb-with-coordinating-adnominal-use","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topics":["topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--adverb-diagnostics"],"statement":{"en":"The word usa is basically an adverb but can be used adnominally in repetitive coordination.","ja":"usa は基本的には副詞であるが、反復並列構文において連体詞的にも用いられる。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/saru"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["usa"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0283-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--negatives-and-prohibitives-are-adverbs","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topics":["topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--adverb-diagnostics"],"statement":{"en":"Negative and prohibitive words such as somo and iteki are adverbs that precede the verb phrase they modify.","ja":"somo や iteki などの否定詞・禁止詞は、被修飾動詞句に先行する副詞である。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["somo","iteki"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0362-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--shizunai-adverbial-adjuncts-free-forms","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topics":["topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--adverb-diagnostics"],"statement":{"en":"Conjunctions, interjections, and adverbs in Shizunai are free forms functioning syntactically as adverbial adjuncts that cannot serve as relational adjuncts.","ja":"静内方言における接続詞・感動詞・副詞はいずれも副詞的付加語として機能する自立形式であり、関係付加語にはなれない。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0070-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"refines","claim":"claim:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--free-adverbial-adjuncts-modify-sentences","differs_in":"scope","note":"Refsing formulates the adjunct status of adverbs, conjunctions, and interjections specifically for Shizunai with the relational restriction, and more generally for Ainu."}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--free-adverbial-adjuncts-modify-sentences","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topics":["topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--adverb-diagnostics"],"statement":{"en":"Conjunctions, interjections, and adverbs are free forms that may function as adverbial adjuncts modifying whole sentences.","ja":"接続詞、間投詞、副詞はいずれも遊離形式であり、連用付加語として文全体を修飾することができる。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0122-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--definition-of-adverbial-adjuncts-in-shizunai","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topics":["topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--adverb-diagnostics"],"statement":{"en":"Adjuncts that are not subjects, objects, case-marked, or quotations are categorized as adverbial adjuncts to the predicate.","ja":"主語、目的語、格標示要素、引用のいずれでもない付加詞は、述語に対する副詞的付加詞として扱われる。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0266-09","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--postpositional-adverbs-independent-use","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topics":["topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--adverb-diagnostics"],"statement":{"en":"Postpositional adverbs express meanings similar to case particles but can also be used independently.","ja":"後置副詞は格助詞と類似した意味を表すが、単独でも用いることができる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0020-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--arity-distinction-among-non-predicative-classes","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topics":["topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--diagnostics"],"statement":{"en":"Adverbs, adnominals, interjections, auxiliary verbs, and non-case particles have an arity of 0, whereas postpositional adverbs and case particles have an arity of +1.","ja":"副詞、連体詞、間投詞、助動詞、格助詞以外の助詞のアリティは 0 であり、後置副詞と格助詞のアリティは +1 である。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["pirkano","eytasa","ani","tura","tan","sine","iyairaykere","uwa","rusuy","pa","ta","un"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0363-06","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--interjections-syntactically-independent-sentences","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topics":["topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--interjection-diagnostics"],"statement":{"en":"Interjections have no syntactic relation with other elements and form independent sentences on their own.","ja":"間投詞は他の要素と統語的関係を持たず、それ自体で独立した文をなす。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0114-05","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--shizunai-three-way-lexical-division","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topics":["topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--inventory"],"statement":{"en":"The lexicon of Shizunai Ainu is initially divided into three major categories: nominals, verbals, and clitics.","ja":"静内アイヌ語の語彙は、まず名詞類、動詞類、接語類の3大グループに区分される。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:majewicz2022@handbook-epub/l0025-02","stance":"reports"},{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0068-05","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--seven-word-classes-classification","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topics":["topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--inventory"],"statement":{"en":"Ainu words are classified on syntactic grounds into seven parts of speech: nouns, verbs, adverbs, prenominals, interjections, auxiliary verbs, and particles.","ja":"統語的特徴のセットに基づき、アイヌ語の品詞は名詞、動詞、副詞、連体詞、間投詞、助動詞、助詞の7種に分類される。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2022pos@handbook-epub/l0090-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"contrasts","claim":"claim:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--six-major-parts-of-speech-classification","differs_in":"framework","note":"Nakagawa presents an inventory of seven parts of speech in his 2022 description and six major word classes in 2024."}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--six-major-parts-of-speech-classification","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topics":["topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--inventory"],"statement":{"en":"Based on grammatical role and formal frame, Ainu words can be classified into six major parts of speech.","ja":"文中の文法的役割と形の上での枠組みに基づき、アイヌ語の品詞は大別して6つに分類できる。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0113-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--nakagawa-five-particle-classes","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topics":["topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--inventory"],"statement":{"en":"Particles in Ainu fall into five functional classes: case particles, conjunctive particles, adverbial particles, sentence-final particles, and auxiliary verbs.","ja":"アイヌ語の助詞は、格助詞、接続助詞、副助詞、終助詞、助動詞の5種に分類される。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0114-11","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0292-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--bound-forms-historically-independent-words","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topics":["topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--inventory"],"statement":{"en":"Seemingly bound forms such as case suffixes, noun prefixes, and auxiliaries are historically independent words that assumed less independent roles.","ja":"格接尾辞や助動詞などの拘束形式に見えるものは、歴史的には自立性を低めた自立語である。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0014-01","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--kindaichi-personal-affixation-criterion-ainu","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topics":["topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--inventory"],"statement":{"en":"Kindaichi proposed classifying Ainu word classes according to whether words can combine with personal affixes.","ja":"金田一は、アイヌ語の品詞分類の基礎として人称接辞と結合できるか否かで分類することを提案した。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0014-02","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[{"kind":"refines","claim":"claim:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--kindaichi-personal-affixation-criterion-hokkaido","differs_in":"scope","note":"Kindaichi's affixation criterion is cited at pan-Ainu and Hokkaido-specific scopes."}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--kindaichi-personal-affixation-criterion-hokkaido","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topics":["topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--inventory"],"statement":{"en":"Kindaichi suggested dividing Hokkaido Ainu words into those that combine with personal affixes and those that do not.","ja":"金田一は、北海道アイヌ語の品詞分類として人称接辞と結合しうる語と結合しえない語への二分を提案した。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0015-01","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--absence-of-inflectional-conjugation","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topics":["topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--inventory"],"statement":{"en":"Ainu has no conjugations or other inflectional morphological mechanisms that alter the basic form of a word.","ja":"アイヌ語には、語の基本形を変化させる活用などの語形変化手段が存在しない。"},"type":"absence","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0016-07","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0017-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--ainu-word-class-inventory-resembles-japanese","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topics":["topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--inventory"],"statement":{"en":"The inventory of word classes in Ainu is similar to that of Japanese.","ja":"アイヌ語の品詞の種類は日本語と似ている。"},"type":"other","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0019-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--chiri-first-proposed-no-adjective-class","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topics":["topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--no-adjective"],"statement":{"en":"Chiri Mashiho's 1942 study was the first to propose that there is no need to distinguish verbs from adjectives in Ainu.","ja":"知里真志保（1942）はアイヌ語において動詞と形容詞を区別する必要がないことを初めて主張した。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0081-01","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--no-independent-adjective-class-in-ainu","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topics":["topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--no-adjective"],"statement":{"en":"There is no need to posit an independent word class of adjectives in Ainu.","ja":"アイヌ語において独立した品詞としての形容詞クラスを設ける必要はない。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:shibatani1990@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0018-07","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"supports","claim":"claim:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--chiri-first-proposed-no-adjective-class","differs_in":null,"note":"Shibatani asserts the no-adjective analysis which Nakagawa notes was pioneered by Chiri."}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--definition-of-nouns-as-predicate-arguments","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topics":["topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--noun-diagnostics"],"statement":{"en":"Nouns are defined as elements that form noun phrases capable of serving as arguments (subject or object) to a predicate.","ja":"名詞は名詞句を形成して述語の項（主語や目的語）になりうる要素として定義される。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2022pos@handbook-epub/l0092-01","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0211-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--noun-distributional-and-affixal-properties","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topics":["topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--noun-diagnostics"],"statement":{"en":"Nouns in Ainu do not serve as predicates, serve as verb arguments, and take at most one personal affix.","ja":"アイヌ語の名詞は述語にならず、動詞の項になり、人称接辞をとる場合は最大ひとつとる。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0114-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--okkay-not-independent-noun-in-saru-chitose","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topics":["topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--noun-diagnostics"],"statement":{"en":"In the Saru and Chitose dialects, okkay is not used as an independent noun.","ja":"沙流・千歳方言では okkay は自立した名詞としては用いられない。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/saru","doculect:hokkaido/chitose"],"quantifier":"specific","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["okkay"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0265-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--definition-of-nominals-non-predicative-free-forms","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topics":["topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--noun-diagnostics"],"statement":{"en":"In Refsing's analysis, nominals are defined as any free forms that cannot function as predicates.","ja":"レフシングの分析において、名詞類（nominals）は述語になり得ないすべての自立形式として定義される。"},"type":"terminology","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0038-02","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0068-06","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--noun-prefixes-strictly-adjacent-and-restricted","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topics":["topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--noun-diagnostics"],"statement":{"en":"Noun prefixes are strictly adjacent to their head nouns and restricted to specific noun subclasses, unlike adnouns.","ja":"名詞接頭辞は連体詞と異なり先行する名詞に密接に結合し、その分布は特定の名詞群に限定される。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0148-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--noun-suffixes-preserve-nominal-status","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topics":["topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--noun-diagnostics"],"statement":{"en":"Noun suffixes extend nominals without altering their syntactic function or nominal status.","ja":"名詞接尾辞は名詞類を拡張するが、その統語的機能や名詞類としての地位を変化させない。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0152-05","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--absence-of-case-inflection-and-gender-in-nouns","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topics":["topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics","topic:nominal/word-class-inventory-and-diagnostics--noun-diagnostics"],"statement":{"en":"Ainu nouns exhibit neither case inflection nor grammatical gender distinctions.","ja":"アイヌ語の名詞には格屈折も文法性の区別も存在しない。"},"type":"absence","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:shibatani1990@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0024-13","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
